<Slide style={{ width: '1280px', height: '720px', background: '#FFFFFF', position: 'relative', fontFamily: 'Source Han Sans, Noto Sans CJK SC, sans-serif' }}>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, left: 0, width: '100%', height: 60, background: '#330662' }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', padding: '14px 60px' }}>Where this is going</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 100, left: 60, width: 700, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 16 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#57068C', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2 }}>WHAT THE NEXT GENERATION OF TOOLS SHOULD ANSWER</Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 40, height: 3, background: '#57068C' }} />
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.55 }}>
      Three trends are already underway. A fourth, more speculative one, may matter more for pedagogy than any of them.
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ marginTop: 8, padding: 18, background: '#F6F1FA', borderLeft: '4px solid #57068C', flexDirection: 'column', gap: 8 }}>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#57068C', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2 }}>A SHIFT WE SHOULD NAME</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.5, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>
        From "AI-assisted game making" to <span style={{ color: '#330662' }}>systematic expression as a literacy</span> for the AI era.
      </Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.55 }}>
        When making a game is easy, the scarce skill is asking a precise question of an experience. Game design is a natural training ground — and a teachable, accountable one, if the workflow is structured for it.
      </Text>
    </Box>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 100, right: 60, width: 440, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 14 }}>
    {[
      { tag: 'TREND 1', t: 'Lower floor', d: 'Generation tools lower the bar to a playable demo. More people will try, and more will produce something.' },
      { tag: 'TREND 2', t: 'A growing case library', d: 'Classrooms and indie teams leave a trail of system descriptions and process logs. The field gets a corpus to study.' },
      { tag: 'TREND 3', t: 'Specialized, one-stop tools', d: 'Generic IDEs hit a ceiling on complete games. Purpose-built engines — blueprint as source of truth, embedded playtest — are the natural next step.' },
    ].map((row, i) => (
      <Box key={i} style={{ flex: 1, padding: 16, background: '#FAF8FC', border: '1px solid #E4DCEC', borderRadius: 8, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 6 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 11, color: '#57068C', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2 }}>{row.tag}</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#330662' }}>{row.t}</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>{row.d}</Text>
      </Box>
    ))}
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 680, left: 60, right: 60, flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>Xingchen Zhang · NYU Shanghai · XJTLU 2026 · Panel 11</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#57068C', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>15 / 16</Text>
  </Box>
</Slide>
